  "title": "# Banner editor (URGENT, top priority, Opus) Brett Nov 3 2026 (voice): \"Build me a banner editor ri…",
  "asked": "# Banner editor (URGENT, top priority, Opus) Brett Nov 3 2026 (voice): \"Build me a banner editor right away, top of the queue, I need it now.\" He needs to remove widgets from his banner. Open it by long-press (hold down) on the banner on touch, and right-click on the banner -> context menu -> Edit banner on desktop. In edit mode he drags and drops widgets, which snap into place; he can remove any widget. If the agent cap queue holds this build, it goes FIRST (priority urgent): `node framework/cli/agent-slots.mjs` priority, per the agent-cap rules. Check first what exists: banner asset type / banner engine (framework/core/engines, framework/schemas/asset-types.json), BannerGroup.tsx, the layout designer, any banner settings, the activity banner widgets. Reuse; don't build a second banner system. Do: 1. Edit banner mode in the framework banner (every app on the framework: console, axHub web, AmberX, Molly): entered by long-press on touch and right-click -> Edit banner on desktop (also a command `banner.edit` and in Settings > Appearance). Exit with Done / Esc. 2. In edit mode: drag and drop widgets with snap (snap slots/zones left, centre, right, ordered), remove a widget (x on each, or drag off), add widgets back from a palette of every available banner widget, reset to default. 3. Save as data: the banner arrangement is a hot-swappable asset / setting saved through the axHub appearance document so every app follows (look comes from axHub only). Undo for the last change. 4. Phone: works at 412 wide, big touch targets. 5. Tests (engine + fixture if the banner engine changes), check-theme, check-controls, help pack + tooltips, UI Review desktop + phone shots (--group \"banner-editor - <Mon D h:mm AM/PM>\"). Rules: one session, no sub-agents. Tokens only (--fx-*), framework controls, no var() fallbacks. Reference engine changed -> regenerate framework/spec/fixtures; Kotlin twin deferred in PORTING.md (Android on hold). Patches paused: don't touch it. Add a THREADS.md row (profile urgent) and update each step. Commit + push branch claude/banner-editor often; open the PR at the end (push banner merges it). Watch live: Brett can watch the screen you are changing hot-render in the console. Whenever you start work on a screen or element, run `node framework/cli/axf.mjs focus <app> [route] [css-selector] --note \"<what you are changing>\"` (apps: console-web, axhub-web, amberx-droid, patches-web, walkthrough-studio, demo, framework, console, axhub-android, voicevault). Agent cap: heavy steps (pnpm/npm/vite builds, docker node:22 test runs, Playwright) share a VPS-wide lock. Run each one as `node /opt/axf/deploy/../framework/cli/agent-slots.mjs heavy -- <command>` so only a few run at once.",
